    description: "Residual of INV-fikoh (PR #1322). ADR-0061 ruling 5: '--no-default-overlays omits community rows from every family'. The verify step now honours it (io overlays, taint derivation, community taint files, community function summaries). The ANALYSIS stage does not: survey/sketch build the graph with the 99 community frameworks/ files, library_signatures/python-django.yaml, dataflow_patterns/python-pyyaml.yaml, and analyzers that build lookup tables from community io rows (py.py:683, haskell.py:699,813 per the original INV-fikoh note; not re-measured). The flag is not an option of the analysis commands, and verify-claims may read a cached graph, so this needs a design decision: an analysis-level flag that becomes part of the cache key, or a stated limit. Decide with WI-hipun (which measures whether frameworks/dataflow rows can make a verdict cleaner at all)."  # e770
    fields: {}  # e770
